  "factor_definition": {
    "name": "intraday_close_range_occupancy_entropy_10b",
    "direction": "higher",
    "formula": "Across the 240 selected closes, let x_i=log(close_i), x_min=min(x), x_max=max(x), and z_i=(x_i-x_min)/(x_max-x_min). Assign b_i=min(floor(10*z_i),9), let p_j=count(b_i=j)/240 for j=0..9, and return -sum_{j:p_j>0}(p_j*log(p_j))/log(10).",
    "economic_hypothesis": "Broad occupation of the completed-session relative close-price range is consistent with distributed two-sided price discovery rather than a fleeting excursion or terminal congestion, potentially leaving a more resilient close-known state for the next-open-to-third-close horizon.",
